title: A Firmer Hand
subtitle: The Chancellor's allies are preparing the ground.
tags: event
view-if: pal_chancellor and emergency_powers >= 7 and not empire_warned and not finale and not game_ending
priority: 4
new-page: true
face-image: img/ev_chancellery.svg
on-arrival: empire_warned = 1

= A Firmer Hand

The Chancellor now holds powers no Chancellor has held since the Ruusan Reformation. In the Senate's corridors his allies speak openly of a "more secure and stable order", and of how tiresome it is to renew the emergency every year.

*If his powers reach **8** while the Senate's resolve is below **5**, the next crisis could be the excuse he needs to proclaim a new order. That would end the Republic, and the game, before the war is over.*

- @rally: Rally the Senate against him.
- @sunset: Force a sunset review now.
- @wait: There is nothing to be done yet.

@rally
subtitle: −1 political capital; Senate resolve rises.
choose-if: capital >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Needs 1 political capital.
on-arrival: capital -= 1; senate_resolve += 1.5; pal_relation -= 5

Caucus senators speak against "the creeping crown" in every debate for a month. The galleries listen.

@sunset
view-if: emergency_sunset
subtitle: The sunset clause forces a vote: two powers lapse.
on-arrival: emergency_powers -= 2; senate_resolve += 0.5; pal_relation -= 8

The Caucus invokes the Sunset Amendment. Two of the Chancellor's powers lapse before his allies can renew them.

@wait

The Caucus watches, and waits.
